<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Analysis of IBCircuit</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Proof of IBCircuit Objective</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We justify the above formulation through the following derivation. Let <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> be a subset of <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is independent to <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math>. Denote <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> as the noisy subset of <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math> determined by injected noise, if we select the circuit <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> by dropping <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the following inequality holds:</p>
<table id="A1.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(\mathcal{G}_{s};\mathcal{C})\leq I(\mathcal{G}_{s};\hat{\mathcal{G}})\leq I(\mathcal{G};\hat{\mathcal{G}})-I(Y;\hat{\mathcal{G}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(\mathcal{G}_{s};\mathcal{C})\leq I(\mathcal{G}_{s};\hat{\mathcal{G}})\leq I(\mathcal{G};\hat{\mathcal{G}})-I(Y;\hat{\mathcal{G}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This equation indicates when setting <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=1</annotation></semantics></math> in Eq. (<a href="#S4.E8" title="Equation 8 ‣ 4.4 Objective for Training ‣ 4 IBCircuit ‣ IBCircuit: Towards Holistic Circuit Discovery with Information Bottleneck" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>), the IBCircuit objective upper bounds the mutual information of <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, optimizing the IBCircuit objective encourages <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> to be less related to components in <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> which are irrelevant to <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We follow the proof in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yu et al., 2022</a>)</cite>. Suppose <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy the Markov condition <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Y,\mathcal{G}_{s})\rightarrow\mathcal{G}\rightarrow\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Y,\mathcal{G}_{s})\rightarrow\mathcal{G}\rightarrow\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Achille and Soatto, 2018a</a>)</cite>. Then we have the following inequality:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(\mathcal{C};\mathcal{G})\geq I(\mathcal{C};Y,\mathcal{G}_{s})=I(\mathcal{C};\mathcal{G}_{s})+I(\mathcal{C};Y|\mathcal{G}_{s})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(\mathcal{C};\mathcal{G})\geq I(\mathcal{C};Y,\mathcal{G}_{s})=I(\mathcal{C};\mathcal{G}_{s})+I(\mathcal{C};Y|\mathcal{G}_{s}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> are independent, we have <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(Y|\mathcal{G}_{s})=H(Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(Y|\mathcal{G}_{s})=H(Y)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(Y|\mathcal{G}_{s},\mathcal{C})\leq H(Y|\mathcal{C})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(Y|\mathcal{G}_{s},\mathcal{C})\leq H(Y|\mathcal{C})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we have:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(\mathcal{C};Y|\mathcal{G}_{s})=H(Y|\mathcal{G}_{s})-H(Y|\mathcal{G}_{s},\mathcal{C})\geq H(Y)-H(Y|\mathcal{C})=I(\mathcal{C};Y)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(\mathcal{C};Y|\mathcal{G}_{s})=H(Y|\mathcal{G}_{s})-H(Y|\mathcal{G}_{s},\mathcal{C})\geq H(Y)-H(Y|\mathcal{C})=I(\mathcal{C};Y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Combine Eq. (<a href="#A1.E15" title="Equation 15 ‣ Proof. ‣ A.1 Proof of IBCircuit Objective ‣ Appendix A Analysis of IBCircuit ‣ IBCircuit: Towards Holistic Circuit Discovery with Information Bottleneck" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>) and Eq. (<a href="#A1.E16" title="Equation 16 ‣ Proof. ‣ A.1 Proof of IBCircuit Objective ‣ Appendix A Analysis of IBCircuit ‣ IBCircuit: Towards Holistic Circuit Discovery with Information Bottleneck" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>), we:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(\mathcal{C};\mathcal{G}_{s})\leq I(\mathcal{C};\mathcal{G})-I(\mathcal{C};Y)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(\mathcal{C};\mathcal{G}_{s})\leq I(\mathcal{C};\mathcal{G})-I(\mathcal{C};Y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy the Markov condition <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Y,\mathcal{G}_{s})\rightarrow\mathcal{G}\rightarrow\hat{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Y,\mathcal{G}_{s})\rightarrow\mathcal{G}\rightarrow\hat{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Achille and Soatto, 2018a</a>)</cite>. Then, combine with Eq. (<a href="#A1.E17" title="Equation 17 ‣ Proof. ‣ A.1 Proof of IBCircuit Objective ‣ Appendix A Analysis of IBCircuit ‣ IBCircuit: Towards Holistic Circuit Discovery with Information Bottleneck" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>) we have:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(\hat{\mathcal{G}};\mathcal{G}_{s})\leq I(\mathcal{G}_{s};\mathcal{G})-I(\hat{\mathcal{G}};Y)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(\hat{\mathcal{G}};\mathcal{G}_{s})\leq I(\mathcal{G}_{s};\mathcal{G})-I(\hat{\mathcal{G}};Y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.SS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text"> is deterministic given <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math>, since we can recover <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math> by combining <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then for the left part in Eq. (<a href="#A1.E18" title="Equation 18 ‣ Proof. ‣ A.1 Proof of IBCircuit Objective ‣ Appendix A Analysis of IBCircuit ‣ IBCircuit: Towards Holistic Circuit Discovery with Information Bottleneck" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>), we have:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(\hat{\mathcal{G}};\mathcal{G}_{s})=I(\mathcal{G}_{\epsilon},\mathcal{C};\mathcal{G}_{s})=I(\mathcal{C};\mathcal{G}s)+I(\mathcal{C};\mathcal{G}_{\epsilon}|\mathcal{G}_{s})\geq I(\mathcal{C};\mathcal{G}_{s})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(\hat{\mathcal{G}};\mathcal{G}_{s})=I(\mathcal{G}_{\epsilon},\mathcal{C};\mathcal{G}_{s})=I(\mathcal{C};\mathcal{G}s)+I(\mathcal{C};\mathcal{G}_{\epsilon}|\mathcal{G}_{s})\geq I(\mathcal{C};\mathcal{G}_{s})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, by combining Eq. (<a href="#A1.E18" title="Equation 18 ‣ Proof. ‣ A.1 Proof of IBCircuit Objective ‣ Appendix A Analysis of IBCircuit ‣ IBCircuit: Towards Holistic Circuit Discovery with Information Bottleneck" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>) and Eq. (<a href="#A1.E19" title="Equation 19 ‣ Proof. ‣ A.1 Proof of IBCircuit Objective ‣ Appendix A Analysis of IBCircuit ‣ IBCircuit: Towards Holistic Circuit Discovery with Information Bottleneck" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>) we have the follow inequality:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(\mathcal{C};\mathcal{G}_{s})\leq I(\hat{\mathcal{G}};\mathcal{G}_{s})\leq I(\hat{\mathcal{G}};\mathcal{G})-I(\hat{\mathcal{G}};Y)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(\mathcal{C};\mathcal{G}_{s})\leq I(\hat{\mathcal{G}};\mathcal{G}_{s})\leq I(\hat{\mathcal{G}};\mathcal{G})-I(\hat{\mathcal{G}};Y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">which proofs Eq. (<a href="#A1.E14" title="Equation 14 ‣ A.1 Proof of IBCircuit Objective ‣ Appendix A Analysis of IBCircuit ‣ IBCircuit: Towards Holistic Circuit Discovery with Information Bottleneck" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Derivation of MI Loss</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Kullback-Leibler (KL) divergence is a measure of how one probability distribution diverges from a second, expected probability distribution. In this section, we derive the KL divergence formula between two Gaussian distributions <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and further calculate the average KL divergence over a batch of data.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.2.1 </span>KL Divergence Formula</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given two Gaussian distributions: <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}:\mathcal{N}(\mu_{i},\sigma_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}:\mathcal{N}(\mu_{i},\sigma_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{i}:\mathcal{N}(\lambda_{i}h_{i}+(1-\lambda_{i})\mu_{i},(1-\lambda_{i})\sigma_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{i}:\mathcal{N}(\lambda_{i}h_{i}+(1-\lambda_{i})\mu_{i},(1-\lambda_{i})\sigma_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>. The KL divergence <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\text{KL}}(Q_{i}\|P_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\text{KL}}(Q_{i}\|P_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> is given by:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E21.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle D_{\text{KL}}(Q_{i}\|P_{i})=\frac{1}{2}\left(\log\frac{\sigma_{P,i}^{2}}{\sigma_{Q,i}^{2}}+\frac{\sigma_{Q,i}^{2}+(\mu_{Q,i}-\mu_{P,i})^{2}}{\sigma_{P,i}^{2}}-1\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{\text{KL}}(Q_{i}\|P_{i})=\frac{1}{2}\left(\log\frac{\sigma_{P,i}^{2}}{\sigma_{Q,i}^{2}}+\frac{\sigma_{Q,i}^{2}+(\mu_{Q,i}-\mu_{P,i})^{2}}{\sigma_{P,i}^{2}}-1\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Substituting the parameters:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E22.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle D_{\text{KL}}(Q_{i}\|P_{i})=\frac{1}{2}\left(\log\frac{\sigma_{i}^{2}}{(1-\lambda_{i})^{2}\sigma_{i}^{2}}+\frac{(1-\lambda_{i})^{2}\sigma_{i}^{2}+(\lambda_{i}h_{i}+(1-\lambda_{i})\mu_{i}-\mu_{i})^{2}}{\sigma_{i}^{2}}-1\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{\text{KL}}(Q_{i}\|P_{i})=\frac{1}{2}\left(\log\frac{\sigma_{i}^{2}}{(1-\lambda_{i})^{2}\sigma_{i}^{2}}+\frac{(1-\lambda_{i})^{2}\sigma_{i}^{2}+(\lambda_{i}h_{i}+(1-\lambda_{i})\mu_{i}-\mu_{i})^{2}}{\sigma_{i}^{2}}-1\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Simplifying the terms:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle D_{\text{KL}}(Q_{i}\|P_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{\text{KL}}(Q_{i}\|P_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\left(\log\frac{1}{(1-\lambda_{i})^{2}}+\frac{(1-\lambda_{i})^{2}\sigma_{i}^{2}+\lambda_{i}^{2}(h_{i}-\mu_{i})^{2}}{\sigma_{i}^{2}}-1\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\left(\log\frac{1}{(1-\lambda_{i})^{2}}+\frac{(1-\lambda_{i})^{2}\sigma_{i}^{2}+\lambda_{i}^{2}(h_{i}-\mu_{i})^{2}}{\sigma_{i}^{2}}-1\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\log(1-\lambda_{i})+\frac{(1-\lambda_{i})^{2}-1}{2}+\frac{\lambda_{i}^{2}(h_{i}-\mu_{i})^{2}}{2\sigma_{i}^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\log(1-\lambda_{i})+\frac{(1-\lambda_{i})^{2}-1}{2}+\frac{\lambda_{i}^{2}(h_{i}-\mu_{i})^{2}}{2\sigma_{i}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.2.2 </span>Average KL Divergence Over a Batch</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a batch of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> data points, the average KL divergence is:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E25.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle D_{\text{KL}}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}D_{\text{KL}}(Q_{i}\|P_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{\text{KL}}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}D_{\text{KL}}(Q_{i}\|P_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Substituting the expression for <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\text{KL}}(Q_{i}\|P_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\text{KL}}(Q_{i}\|P_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D_{\text{KL}}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\left(-\log(1-\lambda_{i})+\frac{(1-\lambda_{i})^{2}-1}{2}+\frac{\lambda_{i}^{2}(h_{i}-\mu_{i})^{2}}{2\sigma_{i}^{2}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{\text{KL}}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\left(-\log(1-\lambda_{i})+\frac{(1-\lambda_{i})^{2}-1}{2}+\frac{\lambda_{i}^{2}(h_{i}-\mu_{i})^{2}}{2\sigma_{i}^{2}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Breaking down the summation:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E27.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle D_{\text{KL}}=-\sum_{i=1}^{n}\frac{1}{n}\log(1-\lambda_{i})+\sum_{i=1}^{n}\frac{(1-\lambda_{i})^{2}-1}{2n}+\sum_{i=1}^{n}\frac{\lambda_{i}^{2}(h_{i}-\mu_{i})^{2}}{2n\sigma_{i}^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{\text{KL}}=-\sum_{i=1}^{n}\frac{1}{n}\log(1-\lambda_{i})+\sum_{i=1}^{n}\frac{(1-\lambda_{i})^{2}-1}{2n}+\sum_{i=1}^{n}\frac{\lambda_{i}^{2}(h_{i}-\mu_{i})^{2}}{2n\sigma_{i}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Assuming <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A_{\mathcal{G}}=-\sum_{i=1}^{n}(1-\lambda_{i}),B_{\mathcal{G}}=\sum_{i=1}^{n}\frac{\lambda_{i}(h_{i}-\mu_{i})}{\sigma_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\mathcal{G}}=-\sum_{i=1}^{n}(1-\lambda_{i}),B_{\mathcal{G}}=\sum_{i=1}^{n}\frac{\lambda_{i}(h_{i}-\mu_{i})}{\sigma_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D_{\text{KL}}=-\frac{1}{n}\log A_{\mathcal{G}}+\frac{(A_{\mathcal{G}})^{2}-1}{2n}+\frac{B_{\mathcal{G}}^{2}}{2n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{\text{KL}}=-\frac{1}{n}\log A_{\mathcal{G}}+\frac{(A_{\mathcal{G}})^{2}-1}{2n}+\frac{B_{\mathcal{G}}^{2}}{2n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Experimental Setting</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For node-level circuit discovery, we set the learning rate to 0.05, trained for 1300 epochs using the Adam optimizer for IB weights, and set <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> to 1. For edge-level circuit discovery, we set the learning rate to 0.1, trained for 3000 epochs using the Adam optimizer for IB weights with a learning rate warm-up scheduler (200 warm-up steps), and set <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> between 0.01 and 1 to balance the sparsity of the circuit and the KL divergence (see the analysis of the parameter <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> in Section <a href="#S5.SS3" title="5.3 RQ2-Ablation Study ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ IBCircuit: Towards Holistic Circuit Discovery with Information Bottleneck" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a>). To obtain the performance of IBCircuit with fewer edges, we selected higher values of <math id="A2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</article>
</div>
</div>
